            <div xml:id="d561">

                <pb facs="0551" n="461" xml:id="pg461"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/3462</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Russian Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ughet</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-12-14"><hi rendition="#italic">December 14, 1918</hi></date>.
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 16.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Polk</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to you herewith
                    paraphrase of two cables received by the Russian Embassy from Omsk, dated
                    respectively December 8 and 10, the importance of which you will appreciate by
                    their contents.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. Ughet</hi></signed>
                </closer>



